#
# A DIAMOND, not a cycle: this aggregator includes `left/manifest-left.ttl` and
# `right/manifest-right.ttl`, and both include the same `shared/manifest.ttl`. The
# walk terminates, so a cycle check alone would let it through — and every case in
# `shared/` would then be loaded twice and counted twice, inflating the pass
# tally exactly as a doubly-discovered aggregator would.
#
# `manifest::load` refuses a manifest reached twice in one closure by name.
@prefix mf: <http://www.w3.org/2001/sw/DataAccess/tests/test-manifest#> .

<> a mf:Manifest ;
    mf:include (
        <left/manifest-left.ttl>
        <right/manifest-right.ttl>
    ) .
